[20:57:09] [backend] Hi
[20:57:09] [backend] 
[20:57:09] [backend] 
[20:57:09] [backend] Rameez here from Beaconfire. I hope you're doing well!
[20:57:09] [backend] We’re currently hiring for an exciting  Java Software Developer role, and I wanted to reach out to see if you or someone in your network might be interested. This is a fantastic opportunity to work on high-impact projects using modern technologies in a collaborative and growth-oriented environment.
[20:57:09] [backend] 
[20:57:09] [backend] 
[20:57:09] [backend] About the Company
[20:57:09] [backend] 
[20:57:09] [backend] BeaconFire is based in Central NJ, specializing in Software Development, Web Development, and Business Intelligence; looking for candidates with a strong background in Software Engineering or Computer Science for a Java / Software Developer position.
[20:57:09] [backend] 
[20:57:09] [backend] 
[20:57:09] [backend] About the Role
[20:57:09] [backend] 
[20:57:09] [backend] The Java / Software Engineer will be responsible for developing applications and writing scalable, secure, maintainable code that powers our clients’ platforms.
[20:57:09] [backend] 
[20:57:09] [backend] 
[20:57:09] [backend] Responsibilities
[20:57:09] [backend] 
[20:57:09] [backend] Develop applications using Java/JEE (and higher), Angular 2+, React.js, SQL, Spring, HTML5, CSS, JavaScript and TypeScript MongoDb, ExpressJs among other tools.
[20:57:09] [backend] Write scalable, secure, maintainable code that powers our clients’ platforms.
[20:57:09] [backend] Create, deploy and maintain automated system tests.
[20:57:09] [backend] Works with Testers to understand defects opened and resolves them in a timely manner.
[20:57:09] [backend] Support continuous improvement by investigating alternatives and technologies and presenting these for architectural review.
[20:57:09] [backend] Collaborates effectively with other team members to accomplish shared user story and sprint goals.
[20:57:09] [backend] 
[20:57:09] [backend] 
[20:57:09] [backend] Qualifications
[20:57:09] [backend] 
[20:57:09] [backend] Experience in a programming language Java, JavaScript and Python.
[20:57:09] [backend] Decent understanding of the software development life cycle.
[20:57:09] [backend] Basic programming skills using object-oriented programming (OOP) languages with in-depth knowledge of common APIs and data structures like Collections, Maps, lists, Sets etc.
[20:57:09] [backend] Knowledge of relational databases (e.g. SQL Server, Oracle) basic SQL query language skills.
[20:57:09] [backend] 
[20:57:09] [backend] 
[20:57:09] [backend] Required Skills
[20:57:09] [backend] 
[20:57:09] [backend] Master’s Degree in Computer Science (CS).
[20:57:09] [backend] 0-1 year of practical experience in Java coding.
[20:57:09] [backend] Experience using Spring, Maven and Angular frameworks, HTML, CSS.
[20:57:09] [backend] Knowledge with other contemporary Java technologies (e.g. Weblogic, RabbitMQ, Tomcat, etc.).
[20:57:09] [backend] Knowledge of JSP, J2EE, and JDBC.
[20:57:09] [backend] If you're currently exploring opportunities or open to learning more, I’d love to connect. Please feel free to share your updated resume or reach out directly at rameezk@beaconfireinc.com.
[20:57:09] [backend] 
[20:57:09] [backend] Looking forward to hearing from you!
[20:57:09] [backend] 
