[21:01:40] [backend]     "answer": "At Morgan Stanley, I designed Spring Boot REST endpoints by separating controller, service, and repository layers so each change stayed localized and testable. For performance, I reduced unnecessary payload and query overhead, then validated improvements through endpoint-level testing in our sprint cycle. I also aligned API contracts and versioning with frontend teams so React and Angular integration stayed stable. That combination helped us improve response behavior while keeping the codebase easier to maintain."
