[21:01:40] [backend]     "answer": "I choose List when order and duplicates matter, Set when uniqueness is the priority, and Map when I need fast key-based lookup. In Java services, I most commonly use ArrayList for ordered transformations, HashSet for duplicate checks, and HashMap for assembling response data. I pick implementations based on access pattern first, then tune for readability and performance."
[21:01:40] [backend]   },
