[21:01:40] [backend]     "answer": "In Spring, dependency injection means the framework provides object dependencies instead of me creating them manually, which keeps components loosely coupled. In my Spring Boot work, I prefer constructor injection for services because it makes dependencies explicit and easier to unit test with Mockito. In enterprise applications, this improves maintainability and lets teams evolve modules without breaking unrelated parts."
[21:01:40] [backend]   },
