[21:01:40] [backend]     "answer": "I start by confirming whether the delay is in application logic or the SQL call using endpoint timing and logs. Then I inspect the query plan, check indexing, and look for N+1 patterns or over-fetching from the ORM layer. In Spring services, I usually improve this with tighter query shape, pagination, and only selecting required fields, then validate with tests before release. That is similar to the performance tuning approach I used in my Morgan Stanley backend work."
[21:01:40] [backend]   },
[21:01:40] [backend]   {
