[13:07:51] [backend] Use the prepared answer only as support context; do not repeat it verbatim.
[13:07:51] [backend] Prepared reference answer: I use a List when order matters and duplicates are fine, a Set when uniqueness is required, and a Map when I need fast key-value access. ArrayList is efficient for indexed reads but costly for middle inserts, while HashSet and HashMap usually give constant-time add and lookup without ordering guarantees. In my schema-mapping pipeline work, sets and maps were useful for duplicate handling and fast matching during JSON correction.
