[14:21:17] [backend]     "type": "concept_knowledge",
[14:21:17] [backend]     "best_resume_match": "Java backend development and API implementation in enterprise applications",
[14:21:17] [backend]     "answer": "List is used when order and index-based access matter, and duplicates are allowed; ArrayList gives fast reads and appends but costly middle inserts. Set is used when uniqueness is required, with HashSet offering average constant-time add and contains, while TreeSet gives sorted order with logarithmic operations. Map is used for key-value lookups, where HashMap is typically fastest on average and TreeMap is useful when ordered keys are needed."
[14:21:17] [backend]   },
