[14:21:17] [backend]     "best_resume_match": "Spring Boot backend services in enterprise multi-threaded environments",
[14:21:17] [backend]     "answer": "HashMap is not thread-safe, so concurrent updates can lead to race conditions and inconsistent state. ConcurrentHashMap is designed for concurrent access with better synchronization behavior and high read throughput. Thread safety is essential when multiple request threads share mutable maps, such as caches, session-like state, or in-memory lookup structures."
