[18:20:51] [backend] performance gaps, achieve measurable improvement vs inherited performance. At Ardent, this meant 28% lower CPA and
[18:20:51] [backend] 35% more consultations in 90 days. The metric I'd use here: blended CPA improvement and conversion volume growth vs
[18:20:51] [backend] day-one baseline.
[18:20:51] [backend] Months four through six: systematic channel expansion and audience scaling. The metric: new qualified customer
[18:20:51] [backend] acquisition
[18:20:51] [backend] cost (true CAC including all marketing costs) vs LTV. If LTV/CAC is above 4x, the acquisition engine is healthy and
[18:20:51] [backend] scalable. If it's below 3x, I'm in efficiency mode.
