[18:33:01] [backend] Q1. Tell me about yourself — 90 seconds, why are you the Growth Marketing Lead we should hire?
[18:33:01] [backend] COACH: Lead with a credibility anchor number. Benchmark it. Close with explicit value for this company.
[18:33:01] [backend] Leave them thinking: "This person has already solved the problem were hiring for."
[18:33:01] [backend] I'm a performance marketing professional with 5-plus years of paid media experience — and a documented track record of
[18:33:01] [backend] building the measurement and qualification infrastructure that makes campaigns actually scale.
[18:33:01] [backend] At Ardent Technologies in Chicago, I managed Google and Meta Ads for US IVF clinics. Within three months: 35% more
[18:33:01] [backend] patient consultations, 28% lower cost per consultation, 40% higher booking rates. Those results didn't come from tweaking
[18:33:01] [backend] bids — they came from diagnosing that the problem was funnel architecture, not ad performance, and rebuilding the
[18:33:01] [backend] qualification layer before touching a single campaign setting.
[18:33:01] [backend] Before Ardent, I ran Facebook campaigns at 28x-32x ROAS — six to eight times the industry benchmark of 3x-5x —
[18:33:01] [backend] generating $336K to $384K monthly from $12K in spend. That's not a lucky campaign. That's a repeatable system.
[18:33:01] [backend] I'm completing my MS in Marketing Analytics at ISU with a 3.92 GPA, hold 14 certifications, and I build my own Tableau
[18:33:01] [backend] measurement infrastructure — so I don't wait for a data team. My optimization cycles run faster because of it.
[18:33:01] [backend] I'm targeting roles where I can build and operate the demand systems that drive a company's growth. Based on what I know
[18:33:01] [backend] about We Inspect, that's exactly what you need. And that's exactly what I'd bring from day one.
[18:33:01] [backend] Q2. Walk me through your resume. What's the through-line?
[18:33:01] [backend] COACH: Show intentionality — every move pointed toward this role. Close by making the connection explicit.
[18:33:01] [backend] Leave them thinking: "Everything in this persons career was pointing toward this exact role."
[18:33:01] [backend] The through-line is a single obsession: connecting ad spend to revenue outcomes through data — and building the systems
[18:33:01] [backend] that make that connection reliable at scale.
[18:33:01] [backend] It started in India. While completing my BBA, I ran a paid media practice for high-consideration healthcare clients. The
[18:33:01] [backend] defining engagement: IVF clinic campaigns at 28x-32x ROAS — six to eight times the industry average of 3x-5x. That
[18:33:01] [backend] taught me the hardest version of this skill — $12K per patient, weeks-long consideration cycles, no room to optimize for
