[18:33:01] [backend] who first engaged with a Meta awareness ad — before they ever searched on Google — had measurably higher consultation
[18:33:01] [backend] booking rates than cold Google Search leads. That's direct evidence that upper-funnel spend was improving lower-funnel
[18:33:01] [backend] quality, not just adding cost. The mechanism was visible in the data.
[18:33:01] [backend] Holdout testing: suppress awareness campaigns for a defined segment for two weeks and watch whether Search volume
[18:33:01] [backend] holds. It typically drops — and that drop quantifies the incremental contribution of upper-funnel spend. The evidence is
[18:33:01] [backend] now
[18:33:01] [backend] in the language a CFO trusts: "Cutting Meta would have reduced Google-attributed consultations by approximately X, at a
