[18:33:01] [backend] Q121. How do you think about brand awareness versus performance marketing?
[18:33:01] [backend] COACH: Performance-first. Marketing Dollar incrementality test. Brand as natural side effect.
[18:33:01] [backend] Leave them thinking: "Performance marketing first — brand builds as a side effect of doing it well."
[18:33:01] [backend] At Marketing Dollar, I tested whether campaigns were building brand or just capturing demand by pausing all ads for one
[18:33:01] [backend] week. Bookings dropped 70%, proving performance campaigns were the primary demand driver.
[18:33:01] [backend] My philosophy: performance first at 80% focus and budget, brand as force multiplier at 20%. At Ardent, Marketing Dollar,
[18:33:01] [backend] and Stars Wellness, I ran 100% performance because budgets needed measurable ROI. But brand was a natural side effect
[18:33:01] [backend] —
[18:33:01] [backend] after six months of Ardent's campaigns, branded searches increased 80%.
[18:33:01] [backend] The test: "If I cut this budget, would revenue drop within 30 days?" Yes means performance. No means brand. Retargeting
[18:33:01] [backend] bridges both — at Marketing Dollar, 35% of conversions involved view-through attribution.
[18:33:01] [backend] I build the performance engine first, prove ROI, earn trust, then introduce brand investment at 15-20% once core campaigns
[18:33:01] [backend] are mature.
[18:33:01] [backend] Q122. How would you approach marketing if you had unlimited budget?
[18:33:01] [backend] COACH: Unlimited doesn't mean undisciplined. Four phases. Still kill what doesn't work.
[18:33:01] [backend] 
[18:33:01] [backend] Leave them thinking: "More budget doesnt change discipline — it accelerates learning."
[18:33:01] [backend] Unlimited budget doesn't mean unlimited spending — it means I'd test aggressively and scale winners without constraint.
[18:33:01] [backend] Phase one, months 1-3: launch $5,000 tests on 8 channels simultaneously — YouTube, TikTok, Reddit, podcasts,
[18:33:01] [backend] programmatic, CTV alongside core Google and Meta. Identify top 3 winners in 90 days.
[18:33:01] [backend] Phase two, months 4-6: hyper-personalization. Instead of one campaign, create segmented campaigns for different user
[18:33:01] [backend] profiles with tailored messaging.
[18:33:01] [backend] Phase three, months 7-9: content and brand investment. Owned channels — video series, podcasts, SEO content — that
[18:33:01] [backend] compound over time.
[18:33:01] [backend] Phase four, months 10-12: advanced data infrastructure. Attribution platforms, customer data warehouses, predictive
[18:33:01] [backend] analytics.
[18:33:01] [backend] Even with unlimited budget I would NOT spray across channels without testing, chase vanity metrics, or abandon
[18:33:01] [backend] performance marketing. Budget increase doesn't change discipline. It accelerates learning.
[18:33:01] [backend] Q123. How do you make decisions when you have incomplete data?
[18:33:01] [backend] COACH: Ardent Milwaukee expansion. Proxy data + worst-case. Reversible vs irreversible model.
[18:33:01] [backend] Leave them thinking: "Calculated decisions with safety nets rather than waiting for perfect information."
