[18:33:01] [backend] data and worst-case analysis. Month 1: $280 CPA. Month 3: $210, stabilized at 10-12 conversions/month.
[18:33:01] [backend] My framework: gather proxy data — Chicago at $180 CPA, Milwaukee at 22% of Chicago's population, fewer competitors.
[18:33:01] [backend] Calculate worst-case acceptable loss — even at $300 CPA, 7 patients at $12,000 LTV generates $84,000 from $2,200. Start
[18:33:01] [backend] small with kill criteria. Check week 1, not month 3.
[18:33:01] [backend] Mental model: reversible versus irreversible. Launching a test is reversible — pause tomorrow. Rebranding is irreversible
[18:33:01] [backend] —
[18:33:01] [backend] get more data. For reversible decisions, bias toward action with safety nets.
