[18:54:05] [backend] Q55. What's your creative testing framework?
[18:54:05] [backend] COACH: One variable. 14 days minimum. 85% confidence. Priority order of variables matters.
[18:54:05] [backend] Leave them thinking: "This person runs tests that produce learnable signal, not just experiments that produce"
[18:54:05] [backend] noise.'"
[18:54:05] [backend] Most creative testing produces noise, not signal — because the variable isolation is wrong or the run time is too short. At
[18:54:05] [backend] M.A.S.S., this framework produced the messaging insights behind the 60% YoY event participation growth. At Ardent,
[18:54:05] [backend] creative testing contributed to the 35% consultation improvement.
[18:54:05] [backend] One variable at a time — always. I've seen campaigns test headline, visual, and CTA simultaneously and conclude nothing
[18:54:05] [backend] because there's no way to isolate cause and effect. Variable isolation is the discipline that makes testing compound into
[18:54:05] [backend] institutional knowledge rather than one-off data points.
[18:54:05] [backend] Minimum 14-day run time — not 7 days. In healthcare especially, weekday and weekend intent behavior differs
[18:54:05] [backend] significantly.
