[19:11:23] [backend] I build teams in phases that match the budget scale — because the wrong team structure at the wrong budget creates
[19:11:23] [backend] coordination overhead without producing better outcomes.
[19:11:23] [backend] Phase one — under $50K/month: I run everything myself. I invest in tools and automation: Tableau dashboards, workflow
[19:11:23] [backend] templates, automated reporting. This is where I build the systems that will scale, not where I add headcount.
[19:11:23] [backend] Phase two — $50K-$200K/month: first hire is a paid media specialist. Profile: 1-3 years of hands-on Google and Meta
[19:11:23] [backend] experience, demonstrably analytical instincts, growth orientation. Onboarding structure: shadow my workflow weeks one
[19:11:23] [backend] through four, own one campaign with guardrails weeks five through eight, full campaign ownership with weekly
[19:11:23] [backend] performance reviews by week twelve. Structured onboarding produces accountable specialists — not a 90-day observation
[19:11:23] [backend] period that turns into sink-or-swim.
[19:11:23] [backend] Phase three — $200K+/month: add a creative strategist — at that budget, creative velocity becomes the bottleneck. And a
[19:11:23] [backend] dedicated analyst to own data infrastructure so I'm spending time on strategy, not dashboard maintenance.
