[19:11:23] [backend] history of reactive changes that compounded the problem. I need to understand that history before I add to it.
[19:11:23] [backend] Week one — full audit, zero changes: build a complete performance map showing ROAS, CPL, conversion rate, and trend
[19:11:23] [backend] direction for every campaign over the last 90 days. Pull the change history log and read it forensically — what was
[19:11:23] [backend] changed,
[19:11:23] [backend] when, and what happened to performance afterward. Also talk to the sales team. Underperformance at the conversion stage
[19:11:23] [backend] is
[19:11:23] [backend] often a handoff problem, not a media problem — if I optimize the ads without understanding the lead quality issue
[19:11:23] [backend] downstream, I'm solving the wrong problem.
[19:11:23] [backend] 
[19:11:23] [backend] Week two — identify the single highest-leverage fix: not five things. One. Typically: wasted spend on irrelevant search
[19:11:23] [backend] terms, a broken qualification funnel passing unqualified leads downstream, or a budget allocation mismatch where the most
[19:11:23] [backend] efficient campaigns are budget-capped while inefficient ones run freely. I fix that one thing, document the hypothesis
[19:11:23] [backend] explicitly, and set a two-week minimum evaluation window.
[19:11:23] [backend] Weeks three and four — structural improvements: proper match type architecture, comprehensive negative keyword lists,
[19:11:23] [backend] audience segmentation. These are right to do but don't produce immediate results — I sequence them after the
[19:11:23] [backend] highestleverage fix so there's early momentum to point to.
