[19:14:34] [backend] retargeting audience signals. Level two — intent signals: lead form opens, partial form completions, click-to-call events. I
[19:14:34] [backend] import these into Google Ads as micro-conversions to feed smart bidding data during the learning period when final
[19:14:34] [backend] conversions are sparse. Without these, the algorithm has nothing to learn from for the first 4-6 weeks.
[19:14:34] [backend] 
[19:14:34] [backend] Level three — qualified actions: completed form submissions, consultation request confirmations. Primary optimization
[19:14:34] [backend] target for both Google and Meta bidding strategies. Level four — business outcomes: booked consultations, appointments
[19:14:34] [backend] kept, closed deals. These live in Salesforce CRM and connect back to campaign data via UTM parameters — producing
[19:14:34] [backend] true
[19:14:34] [backend] revenue ROAS, not just lead-based ROAS.
