[19:14:34] [backend] Q100. How do you approach launching campaigns in a completely new market or industry?
[19:14:34] [backend] COACH: 5-phase framework. The Ardent healthcare entry story is the most powerful example.
[19:14:34] [backend] Leave them thinking: "This person would not guess their way through a new vertical — they have a systematic"
[19:14:34] [backend] framework for learning fast.'"
[19:14:34] [backend] At Ardent, I entered healthcare marketing — a completely new industry — and went from zero knowledge to 28% below
[19:14:34] [backend] industry CPA benchmarks within 3 months. The framework that made that possible is reproducible in any vertical.
[19:14:34] [backend] Five phases. Phase one — deep research, weeks one to two: customer research before anything else. At Ardent, I spent two
[19:14:34] [backend] weeks reading patient forum threads, watching patient experience videos on YouTube, shadowing consultation calls. The
[19:14:34] [backend] insight: patients said "fertility treatment options" not "assisted reproductive technology." Customer language in ad copy
[19:14:34] [backend] consistently outperforms industry terminology in CTR and Quality Score. Competitive intelligence ran in parallel: analyzed
[19:14:34] [backend] 8
[19:14:34] [backend] competing fertility clinics, identified that all focused on success rates and none emphasized emotional support — that gap
[19:14:34] [backend] became our differentiator.
[19:14:34] [backend] Phase two — hypothesis building: based on research, write testable hypotheses. At Ardent: "Women 28-40 actively
[19:14:34] [backend] researching IVF will be most qualified," "Success rate messaging will outperform cost messaging," "Google Search will
[19:14:34] [backend] outperform Meta for high-intent conversions." These became the test design.
[19:14:34] [backend] Phase three — minimum viable campaigns, weeks three to four: $2,000 test budget across 3 audience segments, 3
[19:14:34] [backend] messaging
[19:14:34] [backend] angles, and 2 channels. Small enough to learn cheaply, structured enough to produce actionable data.
[19:14:34] [backend] Phase four — rapid learning, weeks five through eight: weekly reviews killing what fails, scaling what works. Phase five —
[19:14:34] [backend] scale proven winners, month three onwards: 20% monthly budget increases on validated campaigns.
[19:14:34] [backend] The principle: talk to customers before touching the platform. Then test small, learn fast, scale what the data validates. I'd
[19:14:34] [backend] apply this here.
