[20:00:53] [backend] rates. At Stars Wellness, test cities generated 100 conversions vs 12 in control cities — proving 88% incremental lift.
[20:00:53] [backend] Timebased holdout: turn off all ads for one to two weeks and measure conversion drop. At Ardent, pausing Google Ads for
[20:00:53] [backend] one
[20:00:53] [backend] week dropped weekly consultations from 12 to 4 — proving 67% of consultations were ad-driven. Brand search analysis: if
[20:00:53] [backend] campaigns drive awareness, branded search volume increases. At M.A.S.S., launching Instagram campaigns produced a
[20:00:53] [backend] 60%
[20:00:53] [backend] increase in branded Google searches — proving awareness lift. New vs returning customer split: at Marketing Dollar, 95%
[20:00:53] [backend] of
[20:00:53] [backend] 
[20:00:53] [backend] ad-driven conversions were first-time patients — direct incremental proof. Attribution window analysis: if conversions
[20:00:53] [backend] happen immediately after click, ads may be capturing existing demand; if they take 7-14 days, ads are influencing a
[20:00:53] [backend] decision.
[20:00:53] [backend] I'd design and run an incrementality test at We Inspect within the first 90 days. The result should drive budget allocation
