[20:03:26] [backend] One: define the buying trigger, not the audience. For IVF, the trigger is "we have been trying for over a year" —
[20:03:26] [backend] fundamentally different from "people interested in fertility." Every targeting decision flowed from that distinction.
[20:03:26] [backend] Two: map the full conversion path before touching the ad platform. Ad to landing page to qualification form to consultation
[20:03:26] [backend] booking to sales call to closed deal. I identified the drop-off risk at every stage before building anything. That's why I
[20:03:26] [backend] caught
[20:03:26] [backend] the qualification gap before it cost money.
[20:03:26] [backend] Three: campaign objective by funnel stage. Lead gen objective for cold traffic, conversion objective for warm retargeting
[20:03:26] [backend] once quality signal existed. Using the wrong objective burns budget on the wrong optimization signal.
[20:03:26] [backend] Four: build the qualification layer. High-ticket services cannot afford to send unqualified leads to the sales team. This
[20:03:26] [backend] multistep intent filtering is directly what drove the 40% booking rate improvement at Ardent. Industry standard booking
[20:03:26] [backend] rates in
[20:03:26] [backend] this space are 10-15%. We ran significantly above that.
[20:03:26] [backend] Five: instrument everything before launch. Conversion tracking, UTM parameters, Tableau dashboard live before spending.
