[20:35:53] [backend] A 30-day consideration cycle is not a reason to fly blind — it's a reason to build a richer measurement stack than most
[20:35:53] [backend] advertisers use. Here's how I approach it.
[20:35:53] [backend] I build four levels of conversion tracking — each serving a different purpose.
[20:35:53] [backend] Level one — engagement signals: time on site above 2 minutes, specific page views (process pages, pricing pages), video
[20:35:53] [backend] completions above 50%. These are the earliest intent indicators — too soft to optimize against, but valuable as audience
[20:35:53] [backend] signals for retargeting.
[20:35:53] [backend] Level two — intent signals: lead form opens, partial form completions, click-to-call events. These indicate someone is
[20:35:53] [backend] evaluating seriously. I import these into Google Ads as micro-conversions to feed smart bidding data during the learning
[20:35:53] [backend] period when final conversions are sparse.
