[20:38:26] [backend] performance.
[20:38:26] [backend] My solution: GA4 as the source of truth for cross-channel decisions, not platform-native dashboards. Platform dashboards
[20:38:26] [backend] are
[20:38:26] [backend] useful for within-platform optimization — match types, creative performance, audience testing. They're not reliable for
[20:38:26] [backend] telling you whether Google or Meta deserves more budget.
[20:38:26] [backend] For incremental contribution: holdout tests. Suppress Meta for a defined audience segment for two weeks and watch
[20:38:26] [backend] whether
[20:38:26] [backend] Google Search volume and conversion rates hold. They typically drop — which is evidence that Meta's upper-funnel work
[20:38:26] [backend] is
[20:38:26] [backend] 
[20:38:26] [backend] driving Google-attributable conversions that last-click completely obscures. At Ardent, proving assisted conversion value
