[20:38:26] [backend] with
[20:38:26] [backend] a 2-star average will produce more churn, more negative reviews, and more wasted spend. Every dollar we invest brings in
[20:38:26] [backend] a
[20:38:26] [backend] customer who will amplify the negative signal when they leave. We need to either fix the product issue first or narrow our
[20:38:26] [backend] targeting to the specific use case where reviews are positive." That's a hard conversation. It's also the most important one —
[20:38:26] [backend] and avoiding it is how performance marketers destroy trust by delivering short-term traffic against a long-term brand
[20:38:26] [backend] problem.
[20:38:26] [backend] If the reviews are segment-specific: I narrow targeting aggressively to the customer profile where satisfaction is
[20:38:26] [backend] demonstrably high. Same product, different audience, meaningfully different outcome.
[20:38:26] [backend] If the reviews reflect a past issue that has been genuinely resolved: I address it proactively in ad creative. Specific copy
